    "text": "To determine how many marbles remain in Mr Julien's store, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of marbles sold by the customers.\n2. Subtract the total number of marbles sold from the initial number of marbles in the store.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of marbles sold. Since each of the 20 customers bought 15 marbles, we multiply the number of customers by the number of marbles each customer bought:\n\\[ 20 \\times 15 = 300 \\]\nSo, 300 marbles were sold.\n\nNext, we subtract the number of marbles sold from the initial number of marbles in the store. The store initially had 400 marbles, and 300 marbles were sold, so we perform the subtraction:\n\\[ 400 - 300 = 100 \\]\nTherefore, the number of marbles remaining in the store is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
